{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "id": "kukhnya-s01e17-scene-18",
 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Ты труп  (You Are Dead Meat)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "barinov": "Шеф",
  "senya": "Сеня"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Barinov has come back to Claude Monet furious. He has found Senya's veal rolls on the menu of the rival restaurant, and he is sure there has been a leak. He goes straight for Senya. Here are Barinov's questions in Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты был там?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Нет, конечно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Рулеты из телятины с ветчиной.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Я не понимаю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты отдал им наш рецепт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Я ничего им не давал.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ну, Сеня, ты труп.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Шеф, это не я!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Кто тогда?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Может быть, Федя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я тебе не верю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Честное слово!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now the questions Barinov fires at Senya, slowly.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты был там?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Were you there?' \"Byl\" is \"was\" for a man. \"Ty byl tam?\" is a plain statement turned into a question by the voice.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Нет, конечно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, of course not.' \"Konechno\" is \"of course\", and the \"net\" in front turns it into \"of course not\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Рулеты из телятины с ветчиной.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Veal rolls with ham.' \"Iz telyatiny\" is \"made of veal\": \"telyatina\" becomes \"telyatiny\" after \"iz\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Я не понимаю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I don't understand.' \"Ne ponimayu\" is a phrase worth having ready, with \"ne\" right before the action.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты отдал им наш рецепт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You gave them our recipe.' \"Otdal\" means \"handed over\". \"Im\" is \"to them\", the rival kitchen.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Я ничего им не давал.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I didn't give them anything.' Senya answers \"otdal\" with \"ne daval\": he denies giving them anything, ever.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ну, Сеня, ты труп.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, Senya, you're dead meat.' \"Ty trup\" is literally \"you're a corpse\", the same threat as in English.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Шеф, это не я!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Chef, it wasn't me!' \"Eto ne ya\" is literally \"it not I\", with no \"was\" needed.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Кто тогда?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Who, then?' \"Togda\" means \"then\", in the sense of \"in that case\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Может быть, Федя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Maybe Fedya.' \"Mozhet byt\", literally \"may be\", is the everyday \"maybe\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я тебе не верю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I don't believe you.' Russian believes \"to\" a person: \"veryu tebe\", I believe to you.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Честное слово!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Word of honour!' \"Chestnoe slovo\", literally \"honest word\", is how Russians swear they're telling the truth. Here's Barinov and Senya again, from the top.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты был там?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Нет, конечно.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Рулеты из телятины с ветчиной.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Я не понимаю.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты отдал им наш рецепт.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Я ничего им не давал.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ну, Сеня, ты труп.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Шеф, это не я!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Кто тогда?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Может быть, Федя.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я тебе не верю.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Честное слово!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Senya blames Fedya, and Barinov isn't buying it. Hold on to \"ne ponimayu\", I don't understand, which might be the most useful phrase there is. See you next time!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "До свидания!",
   "gap": 0.3
  }
 ],
